# Auto-compaction mid-session: once the branch's measured context tokens
# cross the compaction threshold (internal/harness/compaction.go's
# autoCompact, checked before the next turn's request - the threshold
# itself comes from the current model's budget tier, internal/budget/
# tier.go, not a fixed constant), kiln compacts on its own before sending
# that request - no /compact needed - showing a "Compacting conversation"
# busy label while it runs, and the turn that follows it completes
# normally with the older turns summarized away.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/hooks-auto-compact.yaml

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE /model
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Select model/ 20
KEY down
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Now on faux\/faux-2 · small tier/ 20
TYPE turn one
KEY enter
# Each turn streams ~35k chars as faux chunks; a CI runner needs over 20s
# per turn (finding stream-render-cost-grows-with-reply).
WAITFOR /ENDOFTURN1/ 120
TYPE turn two
KEY enter
WAITFOR /ENDOFTURN2/ 120
TYPE turn three
KEY enter
WAITFOR /ENDOFTURN3/ 120
SHOT three-big-turns-landed
TYPE turn four
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Compacting conversation/ 20
SHOT compacting
WAITFOR /Second pass, after the context was auto-compacted\./ 30
SHOT compacted-and-continued
EXPECT /Second pass, after the context was auto-compacted\./
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
